  "activity": {
    "id": "act_dna_structure_replication",
    "name": "DNA Structure and Replication AR Lab",
    "description": "An exploration of the three-dimensional structure of DNA and the semiconservative process by which it replicates. Students examine the double helix, antiparallel strands, base pairing, and the enzymatic mechanisms at the replication fork.",
    "language": "en",
    "workplace": "wp_molecular_bio_lab",
    "start": "act_1_helix",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "act_1_helix",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "device_ar",
        "location": "place_nucleus",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "The DNA Double Helix",
          "description": "Welcome to the Virtual Nucleus. Before you is a model of the DNA double helix. Observe the two sugar-phosphate backbones spiraling around a common axis. The nitrogenous bases project inward. Note how the structure forms a right-handed helix. Click 'Next' when you are ready to examine the base pairing."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_dna_double_helix",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_audio_intro"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "action",
              "augmentation": "act_2_bases"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "act_1_helix",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "act_2_bases",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "device_ar",
        "location": "place_nucleus",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Complementary Base Pairing",
          "description": "Zooming into the helix interior, observe the complementary base-pairing rules. Adenine (A) always pairs with Thymine (T) via two hydrogen bonds. Guanine (G) pairs with Cytosine (C) via three hydrogen bonds. This specific pairing maintains the uniform diameter of the helix. Say 'bases paired' to continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_base_pairing",
              "poi": "base_pair_target"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "action",
              "augmentation": "act_3_anti"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "act_2_bases",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "act_3_anti",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "device_ar",
        "location": "place_nucleus",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Antiparallel Orientation",
          "description": "Notice the directionality of the strands. The structural asymmetry of the sugar-phosphate backbone means one strand runs in the 5' to 3' direction, while the complementary strand runs 3' to 5'. This antiparallel orientation is crucial for replication. Click 'Next' to begin unwinding."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_antiparallel_arrows",
              "poi": "backbone_target"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "action",
              "augmentation": "act_4_helicase"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "act_3_anti",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "act_4_helicase",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "device_ar",
        "location": "place_bench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Unwinding at the Replication Fork",
          "description": "Pick up the Helicase Tool and bring it to the DNA model. Helicase unwinds the double helix at the replication fork. Notice the single-strand binding proteins stabilizing the exposed parental strands, preventing them from re-annealing."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_helicase_unwinding",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "action",
              "augmentation": "act_5_polymerase"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "thing_helicase",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "act_5_polymerase",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "device_ar",
        "location": "place_bench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Leading and Lagging Strands",
          "description": "Now use the Polymerase Tool. DNA polymerase synthesizes new strands by adding nucleotides only in the 5' to 3' direction. Because the templates are antiparallel, the leading strand is synthesized continuously, while the lagging strand is synthesized discontinuously in Okazaki fragments (later joined by DNA ligase)."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_polymerase_synthesis",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "action",
              "augmentation": "act_6_semi"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "thing_poly",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "act_6_semi",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "device_ar",
        "location": "place_bench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Semiconservative Replication",
          "description": "Replication is complete. Look at the two daughter DNA molecules. Each contains one original parental strand and one newly synthesized strand. This is why DNA replication is described as semiconservative. Click 'Finish' to conclude the lab."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_semiconservative_label",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
